ry French kings began to issue ordinances for the whole kingdom, not just for the principality. Probably the first was Louis VII’s instructions of 1144 banishing Jewish converts to Christianity who had relapsed, and this was followed in 1155 by the constitutions of Soissons, which established the peace of God throughout the kingdom for ten years.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 911, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 828})
