y; even where it was victorious, it still adapted to circumstance. James Russell’s thesis concerning the ‘Germanization’ of Christianity is a good, if flawed, example of how we might focus on religious transformation. Here is something one can maybe identify in Carolingian productions such as the Old Saxon Heliand, which famously transposed Germanic morals and expectations into the story of the Gospels.”'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 885, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 788})
